      "method": {
        "name": "Frozen trajectory with bounded native launch forecasts",
        "summary": "Full-state native-model control: 850 hanging-settle commands, then a retained 650-command trajectory feedback prefix. At the observed launch state, a fixed ordered search selects the first of at most 11 cart-error offsets whose native forecast completes the remaining episode and upright hold; the live episode executes once.",
        "wallClockRealtime": false,
        "usesObservedStateOnly": true,
        "disclosures": [
          "Simulation only. Exact native model and full-state feedback are used. Commands are delivered immediately as clipped float32 normalized actions; feedback arithmetic is binary64.",
          "50 Hz is simulated action cadence, not a wall-clock realtime guarantee. At most 11 internal 650-command forecasts (7,150 forecast command attempts) are permitted at launch, with no physical state overwrite or additional live reset.",
          "The 650 retained gains and offsets are a prefix of the original 700-step zero-terminal design; they were not recomputed with a zero value at step 650.",
          "DEV100 selected the +0.000001 m cart-error profile in two cases; its other 98 cases and all 141 held-out cases selected zero offset. Every selected shadow matched the actual complete suffix byte for byte.",
          "No hardware, post-initialization disturbance, wall-clock realtime, numerical portability, third-party reproduction, or global-priority claim."
        ]
      },
